{"body":"## Problem\n\n`agent.txt` is intended to be a canonical agent-readable entry point, but two things make it harder to trust and inspect:\n\n1. It appears to render as a single long line rather than a readable plain-text contract.\n2. It includes a role bootstrap URL shaped like `https://vibegov.io/roles//BOOTSTRAP.md`, which looks like a missing role placeholder.\n\nBecause agents may consume this file directly, the format and URL pattern should be unambiguous.\n\n## Affected areas\n\nLikely affected file/output:\n\n- `static/agent.txt`\n- any docs that reference the role bootstrap URL pattern\n- any generation script if `agent.txt` is generated\n\n## Recommended fix\n\nMake `agent.txt` multiline and human-inspectable while remaining agent-readable.\n\nReplace the broken role URL with an explicit placeholder pattern such as:\n\n```text\nhttps://vibegov.io/roles/{role}/BOOTSTRAP.md\n```\n\nIf the intended pattern is different, document the exact supported role bootstrap URL shape.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `agent.txt` renders as readable multiline plain text.\n- [ ] No URL contains `roles//BOOTSTRAP.md`.\n- [ ] The role bootstrap URL pattern is explicit and valid.\n- [ ] Agents and humans can determine how to fetch role-specific bootstrap instructions.\n- [ ] Any related docs use the same URL pattern.\n\n## Priority\n\nP0 — canonical agent entrypoint correctness.","id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgxeXa8","title":"Fix agent.txt formatting and role bootstrap URL","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/vibegov.io/issues/155"}
